\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

In this paper, we presented \sysname, a framework for multi-state linear attention. \sysname replaces fixed merging with information-aware dynamic state construction and uses capacity-bounded memory modeling to keep inference cost predictable. By allocating memory resolution based on token-level information variation, \sysname improves representation quality while preserving efficiency. We pre-train \sysname on two linear-attention backbones and evaluate it on 16 datasets across three aspects, where it consistently outperforms state-of-the-art baselines.

